.TH FORGE 1 "May 2026" "forge 0.5.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
forge \- manage symlinked files and portable configuration packs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forge
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]
[\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-interactive\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B forge
manages files through an explicit stage/link workflow. A managed folder stores linked file copies, while original locations become symlinks after
.BR "forge link" .
.PP
The Pack-and-Go commands create portable ZIP archives. Active packs store source paths and BLAKE3 hashes in a manifest; source files are read when
.B forge seal
creates the archive.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Set FORGE_VERBOSE=1 for commands that emit diagnostic output.
.TP
.B \-I, \-\-interactive
Start placeholder interactive mode when no subcommand is provided. The TUI is not implemented yet.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Repository Management
.TP
.B init
[\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-dir\fR \fIDIRECTORY\fR]
Initialize a managed folder. \fB--name\fR sets the folder name and defaults to the directory name. \fB--dir\fR chooses the directory and defaults to the current directory.
.RS
.EX
forge init
forge init --name dotfiles --dir ~/dotfiles
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B list
[\fB\-\-profiles\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-profile\fR \fINAME\fR]
List tracked files. \fB--profiles\fR lists legacy profiles from ~/.forge/profiles. \fB--profile\fR filters tracked files by profile name.
.RS
.EX
forge list
forge list --profile work
forge list --profiles
.EE
.RE
.SS File Management
.TP
.B stage
\fIFILES\fR...
[\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-recursive\fR]
[\fB\-\-depth\fR \fIN\fR]
Stage files or directories before linking. \fB--recursive\fR includes all files below directory arguments. \fB--depth\fR limits directory traversal to N levels.
.RS
.EX
forge stage ~/.vimrc ~/.bashrc
forge stage --recursive ~/.config/nvim
forge stage --depth 2 ~/.config
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B link
[\fIFILES\fR...]
Link staged files. If no files are specified, links all staged files.
.RS
.EX
forge link
forge link ~/.vimrc
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B unstage
[\fIFILES\fR...]
[\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-recursive\fR]
[\fB\-\-depth\fR \fIN\fR]
Deactivate staged records. If no files are specified, unstages all staged files. \fB--recursive\fR matches staged files below directory arguments. \fB--depth\fR limits recursive matching.
.RS
.EX
forge unstage ~/.vimrc
forge unstage --recursive ~/.config/nvim
forge unstage
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B unlink
\fIFILES\fR...
[\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Remove symlinks and restore files from the managed folder while keeping managed copies. \fB--yes\fR skips confirmation.
.RS
.EX
forge unlink ~/.vimrc
forge unlink --yes ~/.bashrc
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B remove
\fIFILES\fR...
[\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Remove files from tracking and delete managed copies while keeping or restoring originals. \fB--yes\fR skips confirmation.
.RS
.EX
forge remove ~/.vimrc
forge remove --yes ~/.old_config
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B delete
\fIFILES\fR...
[\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Delete files from original locations, managed locations, and the database. \fB--yes\fR skips the typed destructive confirmation.
.RS
.EX
forge delete ~/.obsolete_config
forge delete --yes ~/.obsolete_config
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B purge
[\fIFOLDER\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-recursive\fR]
Purge records and managed files for a folder, restoring linked originals first when possible. \fB--recursive\fR processes subfolders and defaults to true in the current CLI.
.RS
.EX
forge purge
forge purge ~/dotfiles
.EE
.RE
.SS Profile Management
.TP
.B new
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fINAME\fR \fIPATH\fR
Create a managed folder for a profile name.
.RS
.EX
forge new --profile work ~/dotfiles/work
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B switch
\fINAME\fR
Switch to a legacy profile from ~/.forge/profiles/NAME.
.RS
.EX
forge switch work
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B profile create
\fINAME\fR
.TQ
.B profile list
.TQ
.B profile switch
\fINAME\fR
Legacy profile commands. Prefer \fBnew\fR, \fBlist --profiles\fR, and \fBswitch\fR.
.SH PACK-AND-GO COMMANDS
.TP
.B start packing
\fISCOPE\fR
Create an active pack manifest at .forge/tmp/pack/SCOPE/manifest.toml.
.RS
.EX
forge start packing my_dotfiles
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B pack
\fIFILES\fR...
[\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-recursive\fR]
[\fB\-\-depth\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Add files to an active pack manifest. \fB--scope\fR selects the pack and defaults to the current directory name. \fB--recursive\fR includes all files below directory arguments. \fB--depth\fR limits traversal. \fB--dry-run\fR previews without writing.
.RS
.EX
forge pack --scope my_dotfiles ~/.vimrc ~/.gitconfig
forge pack --scope my_dotfiles --recursive ~/.config/nvim
forge pack --scope my_dotfiles --depth 2 ~/.config
forge pack --scope my_dotfiles --dry-run --recursive ~/.local/bin
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B check
[\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR]
Verify active pack files against stored BLAKE3 hashes.
.RS
.EX
forge check --scope my_dotfiles
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B seal
[\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR]
Validate an active pack and create .forge/archives/SCOPE-YYYY-MM-DD.zip.
.RS
.EX
forge seal --scope my_dotfiles
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B explain
\fIARCHIVE\fR
[\fB\-\-install\fR]
[\fB\-\-restore\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-target\fR \fIDIRECTORY\fR]
Inspect a sealed pack. \fB--install\fR shows only the install plan. \fB--restore\fR shows only the restore plan. \fB--target\fR previews an install target.
.RS
.EX
forge explain my_dotfiles-2026-05-30.zip
forge explain my_dotfiles-2026-05-30.zip --install --target /tmp/test-home
forge explain my_dotfiles-2026-05-30.zip --restore
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B install
\fIARCHIVE\fR
[\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR]
[\fB\-\-skip\-existing\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-target\fR \fIDIRECTORY\fR]
[\fB\-\-map\-home\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Install a sealed pack. \fB--force\fR overwrites conflicts. \fB--skip-existing\fR skips conflicts and is mutually exclusive with \fB--force\fR. \fB--target\fR installs under a directory. \fB--map-home\fR maps home-directory paths to the current user's home. \fB--dry-run\fR previews without writing.
.RS
.EX
forge install my_dotfiles-2026-05-30.zip
forge install my_dotfiles-2026-05-30.zip --target ~/restored-config
forge install my_dotfiles-2026-05-30.zip --map-home
forge install my_dotfiles-2026-05-30.zip --dry-run --skip-existing
forge install my_dotfiles-2026-05-30.zip --force
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B restore
\fIARCHIVE\fR
[\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR]
[\fB\-\-skip\-existing\fR]
[\fB\-\-test\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Restore a sealed pack. \fB--force\fR overwrites conflicts. \fB--skip-existing\fR skips conflicts and is mutually exclusive with \fB--force\fR. \fB--test\fR restores by filename into the current directory. \fB--dry-run\fR previews without writing.
.RS
.EX
forge restore my_dotfiles-2026-05-30.zip --dry-run
forge restore my_dotfiles-2026-05-30.zip --test
forge restore my_dotfiles-2026-05-30.zip --force
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B repack
[\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR]
[\fIFILES\fR...]
Refresh files in an active pack manifest. \fB--scope\fR selects the pack and defaults to the current directory name.
.RS
.EX
forge repack --scope my_dotfiles ~/.vimrc
forge repack --scope my_dotfiles
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B unpack
\fIFILES\fR...
[\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR]
Remove source paths from an active pack manifest. \fB--scope\fR selects the pack and defaults to the current directory name.
.RS
.EX
forge unpack --scope my_dotfiles ~/.old_config
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.forge/
Global Forge configuration directory.
.TP
.I ~/.forge/config.db
Global SQLite database.
.TP
.I ~/.forge/profiles/
Legacy profile directory.
.TP
.I .forge/
Local managed-folder metadata directory.
.TP
.I .forge/tmp/pack/SCOPE/manifest.toml
Active pack manifest.
.TP
.I .forge/archives/
Sealed pack archive directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Forge generally exits with status 0 on success and nonzero on fatal errors. Some command handlers currently report recoverable operation failures on stderr without terminating the process.
.SH SECURITY
Pack manifests include original paths, relative archive paths, file sizes, timestamps, and BLAKE3 hashes. Use
.B forge explain
and
.B --dry-run
before installing or restoring packs from untrusted sources.
